## Course overview

Physics seeks the most fundamental explanations of how the universe behaves, from everyday motion to quantum and nuclear phenomena. The course pairs mathematical modelling with experimental investigation.

## What you will study

- **Space, time and motion**: kinematics, forces, momentum, and energy.
- **The particulate nature of matter**: thermal physics and gas laws.
- **Wave behaviour**: oscillations, waves, and resonance.
- **Fields**: gravitational, electric, and magnetic fields (extended at HL).
- **Nuclear and quantum physics**: radioactivity and the structure of matter.

